@startuml FINsim Backend Architecture
!theme cerulean
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam DefaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam ArrowColor #8ebef5
skinparam arrowLollipop false

title FINsim Backend Architecture — A/B Testing, 5 Scenarios, 20 Rounds

' ============================================================================
' COMPONENTS
' ============================================================================

package "Entry Point" {
  component [run_simulation.py\n(Orchestrator)] as RunSimulation
  note right of RunSimulation
    Main entry point:
    - Cycles through 5 scenarios (S0-S4)
    - Manages cache check & skip logic
    - Exports JSON results per scenario
  end note
}

package "Caching & File I/O" {
  component [File Cache Manager\n(output/*.json)] as CacheManager
  note right of CacheManager
    Stores scenario results:
    - risultati_S0.json
    - risultati_S1.json
    - ... risultati_S4.json

    Skip logic: If file exists,
    scenario is skipped
  end note
}

package "Simulation Engine (Core)" {
  component [SimulationEngine\n(esegui_round)] as SimEngine
  note bottom of SimEngine
    Orchestrates round loop:
    1. Query active clusters (Neo4j)
    2. Generate strategies (PromotoreAgent)
    3. Persist decisions (DecisioneCommerciale)
    4. Update client reactions
  end note
}

package "Strategy Generation (LLM Layer)" {
  component [PromotoreAgent\nStrategy Generator] as PromAgent
  note bottom of PromAgent
    Generates cluster-specific strategies:
    - Scenario context (rates, liquidity)
    - Bank directive (product focus)
    - Client profiles (risk tolerance)
    Uses: qwen2.5:3b (LIGHT_LLM)
  end note

  component [OllamaClient\nREST Interface] as OllamaClient
  note bottom of OllamaClient
    Local LLM API client:
    - Timeout-aware requests
    - Retry logic + fallback
    - Parameterized prompts
    Endpoint: http://localhost:11434
  end note
}

package "Data Access Layer" {
  component [FinsimSearcher\n(Secure Queries)] as Searcher
  note bottom of Searcher
    Parameterized Neo4j queries:
    - Allowlist validation (labels, rels)
    - Cluster lookup (grid position)
    - Promoter portfolios
    - Scenario state
    Uses: finsim_schema.json
  end note
}

package "Persistent Storage" {
  database [Neo4j\n(5.15 Community)] as NeoDb
  note bottom of NeoDb
    Graph structure:
    - ScenarioMacro (S0-S4)
    - DirettivaBancaria (1 per scenario)
    - Promotori (2: Fixed, Adaptive)
    - Clienti (100 synthetic, 10x10 grid)
    - DecisioneCommerciale (decisions)
  end note
}

package "Output & Results" {
  component [JSON Exporter\n(esporta_json)] as Exporter
  note bottom of Exporter
    Exports scenario results:
    - Round-by-round decisions
    - Trust metrics (avg, distribution)
    - Promoter performance (A/B)
    Format: JSON (UTF-8)
  end note
}

' ============================================================================
' RELATIONSHIPS & FLOW
' ============================================================================

RunSimulation --> CacheManager : "1. Check cache\n(file exists?)"
CacheManager --> RunSimulation : "Skip or Proceed"

RunSimulation --> SimEngine : "2. Execute scenario\n(if not cached)"

SimEngine --> Searcher : "Query clusters,\npromoter data,\nscenario state"

Searcher --> NeoDb : "Parameterized\nCypher queries"
NeoDb --> Searcher : "Node & relationship\nresults"

SimEngine --> PromAgent : "Generate strategy\nfor cluster"

PromAgent --> OllamaClient : "HTTP POST\n(system + user prompt)"
OllamaClient --> PromAgent : "JSON strategy\nresponse"

SimEngine --> NeoDb : "Persist decisions\n(DecisioneCommerciale)"
SimEngine --> NeoDb : "Update client trust\n& satisfaction"

SimEngine --> Exporter : "Collect decisions\n& metrics"
Exporter --> CacheManager : "Write JSON\nto output folder"

' ============================================================================
' LEGEND & NOTES
' ============================================================================

note as Legend
  **A/B Testing Matrix:**
  - 100 clients total
  - Promotore Fisso (Fixed): 50 clients → Benchmark broadcast
  - Promotore Adattativo (Adaptive): 50 clients → LLM-driven strategy

  **Scenario Execution:**
  - S0: Baseline Neutral (2.0% rate)
  - S1: Rate Shock (2.5% rate)
  - S2: Acute Crisis (3.0% rate, liquidity crisis)
  - S3: Opportunity (1.8% rate, regulatory pressure)
  - S4: Bifurcation (S0 → pivot at R10)

  **Round Loop (per scenario):**
  - Reset client state (trust ← initial, satisfaction → 0.5)
  - For each round (1..20):
    - For each promoter cluster:
      - Query clients in grid cell
      - Generate strategy (LLM)
      - Calculate client reactions
      - Persist to DB

  **Security Model:**
  ✓ Parameterized Neo4j queries (no f-string injection)
  ✓ Label/relationship allowlist validation
  ✓ Timeout-aware LLM requests
  ✓ Error recovery & continue logic
end note

@enduml
